This preview contains the project's Python Core ML adapter and Swift bridge.
src/dflash_coreml/target.py adapts the packed Hadamard operators and validation
from oMLX's prism_hadamard_qwen35 implementation, distributed under Apache-2.0.
It changes loading to text-only local checkpoints without an app installation.
Upstream: https://github.com/jundot/omlx (Jundot and oMLX contributors).
Copyright (c) 2026 dflash-coreml contributors.
This project is distributed under Apache-2.0; see LICENSE.
It does not bundle Apple frameworks, the rest of MLX/oMLX/dflash-mlx, the official
CandidateSelector implementation, target checkpoints or converted model weights.

The design uses Apple's Core ML APIs and is intended to interoperate with
DFlash2 and MLX. References:
https://github.com/jundot/omlx
https://github.com/z-lab/dflash
https://github.com/bstnxbt/dflash-mlx

Model redistribution requires checking the exact original checkpoint's license
and preserving required attribution. Converted model weights are distributed separately at
https://huggingface.co/uqer1244/Qwen3.8-27B-DFlash2-CoreML.
